---
title: Agent Run Lifecycle — How Context Compounds
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant W as Workflow Trigger
    participant CA as Context Assembler
    participant GS as Context Graph
    participant E as Agent Engine
    participant X as Executor
    participant TB as Tool Broker
    participant TS as Trace Store
    participant TD as Trace Decomposer

    W->>CA: Intent + AgentProfile
    CA->>GS: Query knowledge nodes (Layer 5)
    GS-->>CA: Relevant concepts, insights, patterns
    CA->>GS: Query similar trajectories (Layer 6)
    GS-->>CA: Past decisions with outcomes
    CA-->>CA: Assemble ContextPacket (9 layers)

    CA->>E: ContextPacket
    E-->>E: Propose Plan (with citations)
    E->>X: Structured Plan

    X->>X: Validate schema + policy
    X->>TB: Execute actions
    TB-->>X: ToolCallRecords

    X->>TS: Write DecisionTrace

    TS->>TD: on_trace_completed hook
    TD->>GS: Create TRAJECTORY node
    TD->>GS: Create DECISION_EVENT nodes
    TD->>GS: Update CO_OCCURS_WITH edges
    TD-->>TS: DecompositionResult

    Note over GS: Graph grows with every run.<br/>Next query retrieves<br/>this run's knowledge.
